## Your Task

Write the 7-step causal narrative following the dialectic structure defined in
the system prompt. Track attacker and defender beliefs only when attacker
access is supported; otherwise track the declared structural condition. Be
specific about which structural elements are involved at each step.

Keep one compact paragraph per step (at most two sentences each, roughly 400
words total). Use every declared factor in projection order, and do not bridge
unrelated structural elements or state attacker success without exact typed
capability evidence.

The narrative must realize the projection alignment table in table order. The final scenario step must state the exact ICA type and control action from the table's required reference.

Use the immutable scenario context as the only source of ICA, action, hazard,
loss, constraint, obligation, and capability meaning. Do not introduce a new
primary causal factor beyond the factors declared in the scenario specification.
When reachable_capabilities is empty, explain the existing structural
condition and how an adversary can take advantage of it. Do not invent a new
interface, channel, or privilege. A bounded_assumption must be labelled as
such and may not become structured evidence.

Return the narrative as raw prose text.
